# Postcard
#
# Db major, 3/4, 63 bpm. Bass on the downbeat, chord on beat two, the
# melody entering after the beat — the lilt of a slow waltz that never
# quite starts. Two bars a chord.
#
#   loop  Gbmaj7 | Db/F | Ebm9 | Ab7sus4      IV - I6 - ii9 - Vsus: it
#         never cadences; the sus chord leans back into IV, so the seam
#         of the loop is never heard.
#   B     Bbm9 | Gbmaj7 | Cbmaj7#11 | Ab7sus4 | Bbm9 | Gbmaj7 | Ebm9 | Absus
#         one borrowed chord (Cb, the flat seventh) is the whole surprise
#         budget, and the melody's one climax (Db6) sits on it.
#
# The melody is one motif — a pickup that leaps up a sixth onto a long
# note and sighs down a step — stated, re-coloured over a new chord, then
# answered. Phrase peaks climb Ab5, Bb5, then Db6 once. Phrase endings go
# open (Eb, the 2nd), half-closed (F, the 3rd); only the last statement
# lands on Db, and even then the harmony stays on IV.
#
# Fog to clarity: the first statement is filtered and echoing, the second
# is clear, the last carries an octave halo; the coda keeps only the motif.
#
#   0:00 intro (pads + bass)   0:23 A    1:09 A (clear)   1:55 B
#   2:41 A (halo)              3:27 coda
#
# Effects: the reverb is send-only (pads wet, lead nearly dry, bass dry);
# the lead's space is a dark echo a dotted quarter behind it. No chorus,
# no wow, no vibrato: everything stays in tune.
#
# 63 bpm, 3 beats a bar; bar n starts at beat 3*(n-1).

bpm 63
gate 0.95
tail 10

section INTRO 0..24
section A1 24..72
section A2 72..120
section B 120..168
section A3 168..216
section CODA 216..246

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ lead

track lead vel=0.6 patch=init gain=0.62 echo_send=0.35 reverb_send=0.12
R:24 R:1
# A1 (foggy)
Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.66 Eb5:1@0.55 | Gb5:2@0.66 F5:1@0.58 | Eb5:1@0.55 Db5:2@0.6 | R:1 Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.64 Gb5:1@0.56 | Ab5:2@0.68 Gb5:1@0.58 | Eb5:4@0.6
Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.64 Eb5:1@0.55 | Gb5:1@0.58 Ab5:1@0.62 Bb5:4@0.72 | Ab5:2@0.64 Gb5:1@0.56 | F5:2@0.6 Db5:1@0.52 | Eb5:3@0.58 | F5:4@0.6
# A2 (clear)
Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.66 Eb5:1@0.55 | Gb5:2@0.66 F5:1@0.58 | Eb5:1@0.55 Db5:2@0.6 | R:1 Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.64 Gb5:1@0.56 | Ab5:2@0.68 Gb5:1@0.58 | Eb5:4@0.6
Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.64 Eb5:1@0.55 | Gb5:1@0.58 Ab5:1@0.62 Bb5:4@0.72 | Ab5:2@0.64 Gb5:1@0.56 | F5:2@0.6 Db5:1@0.52 | Eb5:3@0.58 | F5:4@0.6
# B: the motif up a step over Bbm9, sequenced over Gb, the climax on Cb
C5:1@0.52 Ab5:3@0.66 F5:1@0.56 | R:1 Db5:1@0.54 Bb5:3@0.7 Ab5:1@0.58 | Bb5:3@0.68 | Db6:2@0.78 Bb5:1@0.62 | Ab5:2@0.64 Gb5:1@0.56 | Eb5:3@0.58
R:1 Ab4:1@0.48 F5:3@0.6 Db5:1@0.52 | Eb5:2@0.56 Db5:1@0.5 | Bb4:3@0.54 | R:3 | R:1 Bb4:1@0.46 Db5:1@0.5 | Eb5:3@0.56 | R:3
# A3 (with its octave), ending home on Db
R:1
Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.66 Eb5:1@0.55 | Gb5:2@0.66 F5:1@0.58 | Eb5:1@0.55 Db5:2@0.6 | R:1 Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.64 Gb5:1@0.56 | Ab5:2@0.68 Gb5:1@0.58 | Eb5:4@0.6
Ab4:1@0.5 F5:3@0.64 Eb5:1@0.55 | Gb5:1@0.58 Ab5:1@0.62 Bb5:4@0.72 | Ab5:2@0.64 Gb5:1@0.56 | F5:2@0.6 Gb5:1@0.54 | F5:2@0.58 Eb5:1@0.52 | Db5:4@0.6
# coda: the motif alone, slower, left hanging on F over Gbmaj7
R:2 R:3 | R:1 Ab4:2@0.46 | F5:6@0.54 | Eb5:3@0.48 | R:6 | F5:6@0.46
